  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# One-on-one: Nico and Osric\n\n**Date:** May 18\n**Attendees:** Nico Sample, Osric Testcase\n\n## Summary\n\nFortnightly one-on-one. We covered the Harbourline retest plan, Osric's promotion packet, and how he wants to handle the next few weeks at home before his leave.\n\n## Work\n\n- The Harbourline beta milestone slipped a week because the account-linking screen is being reworked after the first round of testing. Osric is comfortable with the new date and has told the client.\n- Osric's promotion packet to senior designer is nearly ready. He wants one more case study in it, ideally the Harbourline onboarding work once the retest is done.\n- I agreed to review the draft packet before the next calibration round.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **Nico Sample** — review Osric's promotion packet by May 29 and send written feedback.\n- **Osric Testcase** — add the Harbourline onboarding case study to the packet after the retest.\n\n## Home and family\n\n- Osric asked to keep Fridays short for the next month. Their son Lowell has swimming lessons straight after school, and Osric and Mercer take turns collecting him.\n- Osric and Mercer's daughter Ivo is starting nursery in September; Mercer is handling the settling-in sessions.\n- Ivo turns five on June 2 and they are having a small party at home that weekend. Osric will be offline that Friday afternoon.\n- Osric is the parent of both Lowell and Ivo, and Mercer is their mother; worth remembering for scheduling around school holidays.\n\n## Wellbeing\n\nOsric said the workload feels manageable now that the Harbourline scope is settled. He is looking forward to the Lisbon trip and has already started the handover notes for Sabin.\n\n## Next one-on-one\n\nIn two weeks, after the Harbourline retest, so we can look at the results and the updated packet together.\n"
  },
